## 2. ROUND-TRIP BYTE IDENTITY on messages carrying unknown fields
#   decode with the capture on, re-encode with the bag, compare with the input.
#   None of the existing vectors test this: today the unknowns are dropped and
#   the re-encode is legitimately shorter.

#   THE ORDERING QUESTION, answered rather than chosen silently: the bag is
#   APPENDED AT THE END of the message. Canonical form ascends by tag, so an
#   unknown tag that sits numerically between two known tags re-encodes in a
#   different ORDER -- same fields, same bytes, different position. The
#   `expected` column says which vectors that applies to, and the gate is
#   agreement with the expectation, not identity.

vector                                           in B  out B bag == input layout ident expected  semantic RT
all four wire types, AFTER every known field       62     62 yes          yes          yes       yes
one unknown BEFORE every known field               10     10 yes          no           no        yes
an unknown tag BETWEEN two known tags (the ordering case)     10     10 yes          no           no        yes
two elements, each with its own unknown field      16     16 yes          yes          yes       yes

